    "body": "_Requested by **Sia**_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Order: independent; safe to merge anytime (follows #427, already in main).\n- Depends on: nothing open.\n- If merged out of order with the DEVONthink stack (#415, #418-#421): they only touch the module table near line 164 of `sp-academic.org`; this PR edits the Citar section, so no conflict is expected.\n\n## What is reverted\n\n- The width fitting is removed from `sp-citations.el` and its doc: `sp-citations--format-candidates` (advice), `--fit-widths`, `--assemble`, `--candidate-width`, `sp-citations-candidate-margin`, `sp-citations-column-priorities`, `sp-citations-column-max-widths`, `sp-citations-prefix-width`, `--indicator-block-width`, and the stretched spaces.\n- This undoes the code of: 1a85a2bf (#406, fit to posframe), db834802 (#409, align and prioritise), 45221b0f (#409, 45-column cap), 5414dc60 (#427, prefix width). Their tests file `tests/sp-citations-columns-test.el` goes too.\n- Not reverted: the `sp-org-tag-groups` entry-type table (#411) and the docs of the BibTeX types.\n\n## What stays, and what is ambiguous\n\n- Kept: faded italic citekey (#405), emoji indicators 🌿️ 📁️ 📝️ 🎓️ with no padding between them (#409), entry-type emoji (#411), and the column order emoji, author, year, title, citekey, keywords.\n- I read \"before the wrapping request\" as before #406, but the layout of #405 used the old coloured L/F/N letters and a different order. I kept the emoji and the order because they are separate asks, not wrapping.\n- With the fitting gone, columns have fixed widths in `citar-templates`, as in #405: type 3, authors 30, year 4, title 60, citekey 45, tags the rest. Longer values are cut. Raise a number there to show more.\n- If you want the full #405 look back (coloured letters, no emoji, old order), say so and I will revert those too.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Pull this branch, restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`), `M-x citar-refresh` (untested by Claude: GUI)\n- [ ] `C-c w b o` (`citar-open`): columns read emoji, authors, year, title, citekey, keywords (untested by Claude)\n- [ ] The citekey shows up to 45 characters and the year is whole\n- [ ] Edge: a long title is cut at 60 columns; the rest of the row stays in place\n- [ ] Regression: indicators 🌿️ 📁️ 📝️ 🎓️ and the entry-type emoji still show; `citar-insert-citation` and `citar-create-note` work\n\n<details><summary>Revert after testing</summary>\n\n- Discard local edits: `git -C ~/dotfiles status`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles restore .` (`git clean -fd` only after checking `git clean -nd`).\n- Back to main: `git -C ~/dotfiles switch main`, then `git -C ~/dotfiles pull`.\n- Optionally delete the test branch locally: `git -C ~/dotfiles branch -D claude/revert-citar-column-fitting` (the remote copy stays until the PR is merged or closed).\n- Restart Emacs (or `M-x sp-reload-modules`) and run `citar-refresh`.\n- No notes or vault files change, so nothing to restore there.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9m8fmtgNiBeMPZDGW)_",
